\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266441} {:answer/id #uuid "55250c42-2129-5ad8-a825-45e36c162fb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "74.0\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266906} {:answer/id #uuid "c1732452-ba86-5b66-9d0f-8ecb8ef36ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "147.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267870} {:answer/id #uuid "dad302c2-78ab-5cef-8a01-c1ccfe0f5687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270.0\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1732452-ba86-5b66-9d0f-8ecb8ef36ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "147.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267870} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc78480b-f21a-58e1-ae11-97412bfc6d2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e15d21c-4fa7-50e9-9890-e404c2c7a6c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-135099" :question/problem "A marble is projected vertically downward from a building with a velocity of $0.3\\,\\text{km/min}.$  It takes the marble $5\\,\\text{s}$ to hit the ground. What is the height of the building? \n\n*Hint: The acceleration due to gravity is $9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula\n\n$$\ns=ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the displacement, measured from the starting position in the direction of the initial motion, $u$ is the initial velocity, $t$ is the time since the beginning of the motion, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.\n\nLet's summarize the information we have:\n\n- We can find the initial velocity of the marble in meters per second as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =0.3\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{min}} \\\\  & =0.3\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{km}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{min}}{60\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =0.3\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{km}}}{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{km}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}{60\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =0.3\\cdot \\frac{1000\\,\\text{m}}{60\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The marble falls for $t=5\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2} \\\\  & =(5)(5)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (9.8)(5)^{2} \\\\  & =25+(4.9)(25) \\\\  & =147.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the building is $147.5\\,\\text{m}$ high."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083384 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c3fb8a8-343a-5046-afce-83db17ec1039" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Initial Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c5bb798-cec3-5a92-9d75-11208ba367e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "61.2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398391} {:answer/id #uuid "4d938cd5-a02b-597a-b438-1708be6fb7f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80.2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398392} {:answer/id #uuid "577131db-9008-56b9-a467-51c63bcf9b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "67\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398393} {:answer/id #uuid "af98f4ef-a70e-5c69-9cbd-4bc71919c6e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75.1\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398394} {:answer/id #uuid "ea7e78d9-3274-5840-9bbb-71ef4bb5921d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70.6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea7e78d9-3274-5840-9bbb-71ef4bb5921d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70.6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398395} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a5589d-c173-52b7-aa4e-ec8dcdd731a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04947b95-8a1f-567f-948f-2de5de86130e" :question/math-academy-id "q-135105" :question/problem "An object is projected vertically down from a height of $0.6\\,\\text{km}$ and hits the ground in $6\\,\\text{s}.$ What was the initial velocity of the object?\n\n*Hint: The acceleration due to gravity is $9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula\n\n$$\ns=ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the displacement, measured from the starting position in the direction of the initial motion, $u$ is the initial velocity, $t$ is the time since the beginning of the motion, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.\n\nLet's summarize the information we have:\n\n- The object falls for $t=6\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n- We can find the distance the object falls in meters as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =0.6\\,\\text{km} \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\text{km}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{km}} \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\cancel{\\text{km}}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{km}}} \\\\  & =0.6\\cdot 1\\,000\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =600\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula and solving for $u,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2} \\\\ (600) & =u(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(9.8)(6)^{2} \\\\ 600 & =6u+176.4 \\\\ 423.6 & =6u \\\\ u & =70.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the initial velocity of the object was $u=70.6\\,\\text{m/s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083384 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c3fb8a8-343a-5046-afce-83db17ec1039" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Initial Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65978ce6-df64-5de6-aeab-42de7c34421a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.4\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267045} {:answer/id #uuid "90f37520-bdc0-5101-8fa8-e439c6fa8a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267434} {:answer/id #uuid "ac8cdabb-612d-5de7-9682-d99f1ee7ee7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.1\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267700} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fca792-de9a-5fdb-86b8-014ceb5d535a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267769} {:answer/id #uuid "c5aa12e3-0532-503a-a1f6-9c28ecc980d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5fca792-de9a-5fdb-86b8-014ceb5d535a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267769} :answer-field/id #uuid "176f199d-1d63-5478-9d6f-26b21b3cd994" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f994d9-de97-52de-9c5c-2b1ac143f4bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-135223" :question/problem "A coin is projected vertically down from a skyscraper with a height of $720\\,\\text{m}.$ It takes $12\\,\\text{s}$ to hit the ground. What was the initial velocity of the coin?\n\n*Hint: The acceleration due to gravity is $9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula\n\n$$\ns=ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the displacement, measured from the starting position in the direction of the initial motion, $u$ is the initial velocity, $t$ is the time since the beginning of the motion, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.\n\nLet's summarize the information we have:\n\n- The coin falls for $t=12\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n- The coin covers the distance of $s=720\\,\\text{m}.$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula and solving for $u,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2} \\\\ (720) & =u(12)+\\frac{1}{2}(9.8)(12)^{2} \\\\ 720 & =12u+705.6 \\\\ 14.4 & =12u \\\\ u & =1.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the initial velocity of the coin was $1.2\\,\\text{m/s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083385 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d441155e-dbcb-598d-afc7-949ee4eddbee" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Time"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c8857b7-5f5d-5457-8dd6-2b4309d575d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400711} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f420ae-7985-53ba-8421-2ceb6b4b4f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400712} {:answer/id #uuid "57bed31e-8ef7-54da-8f39-982e238c1dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400713} {:answer/id #uuid "5fdee401-1c5c-5788-8574-ed2dd56862ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400714} {:answer/id #uuid "75082212-5bbc-5f18-98d7-7d1fb55b442b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57bed31e-8ef7-54da-8f39-982e238c1dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400713} :answer-field/id #uuid "106db307-f502-5d2c-ad7c-d17a4f3844ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "183a141f-bd68-52b7-ae90-0aa68787bc11" :question/math-academy-id "q-135228" :question/problem "A marble is projected vertically downward from a height of $245\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $24.5\\,\\text{m/s}.$ How long will it take for the marble to hit the ground? \n\n*Hint: The acceleration due to gravity is $9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula\n\n$$\ns=ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the displacement, measured from the starting position in the direction of the initial motion, $u$ is the initial velocity, $t$ is the time since the beginning of the motion, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.\n\nLet's summarize the information we have:\n\n- The initial velocity of the marble is $u=24.5\\,\\text{m/s}.$\n\n- The marble covers the distance of $s=245\\,\\text{m}.$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula and solving for $t,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2} \\\\ 245 & =(24.5)t+\\frac{1}{2}(9.8){t}^{2} \\\\ 245 & =24.5t+4.9{t}^{2} \\\\ 50(4.9) & =5(4.9)t+4.9{t}^{2} \\\\ 50\\cancel{(4.9)} & =5\\cancel{(4.9)}t+\\cancel{(4.9)}{t}^{2} \\\\ 50 & =5t+{t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}+5t-50 & =0 \\\\ (t+10)(t-5) & =0 \\\\ t & =-10,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution. Therefore, the marble hits the ground after $t=5$ seconds."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6eea26e0-2a9c-5d4c-91d3-12e7682e1858" :knowledge-point/title "Inverting a Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40964cdf-1fba-5397-b650-220685d4b822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388323} {:answer/id #uuid "afb6e5f1-f54b-5c96-9c80-d6dc9b8da948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388324} {:answer/id #uuid "46fda007-53e3-5bf4-bbf8-aaa74c02fa0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388325} {:answer/id #uuid "3d667efc-6c25-5864-8c74-e9e2e74d3c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388326} {:answer/id #uuid "b475a46a-207d-5a1b-ba81-c4c924a38872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40964cdf-1fba-5397-b650-220685d4b822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388323} :answer-field/id #uuid "f09b45e9-dd8e-565d-ab33-a73e99322450" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df59a1aa-1439-516c-b162-bd4f36cbb04a" :question/math-academy-id "q-135315" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d359337c-4ec2-5100-bdac-d0858619db3b" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Products Containing Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bba42d0-4d22-55d1-bf2a-5afa7f154545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266532} {:answer/id #uuid "6f0dba1e-ebd9-58df-9ff0-a39f534c6156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267118} {:answer/id #uuid "9a78f2b9-be60-5dd9-a1b2-d3dae91c37e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267540} {:answer/id #uuid "a54496d0-737c-5f0e-b323-1106d3723e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267634} {:answer/id #uuid "da3d8464-42f7-59e9-bbc9-ba3a5c255583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bba42d0-4d22-55d1-bf2a-5afa7f154545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266532} :answer-field/id #uuid "464dd787-aac1-5fd3-8b68-a426f70499c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5d3c5f6c-be88-5a7d-88c2-f5f9124aa97d" :question/math-academy-id "q-13533" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6eea26e0-2a9c-5d4c-91d3-12e7682e1858" :knowledge-point/title "Inverting a Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae64e00f-248f-5416-a7d7-f63abd460d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388330} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca42262-1856-5fae-96d8-21a6b1bbb5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388331} {:answer/id #uuid "7891ed69-db39-56d8-9b5d-8c5c52ec5455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388332} {:answer/id #uuid "af60b232-b43d-5148-acd4-6766dd50925f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388333} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d5d26b-c0d3-5eb3-9f7e-65cf2e302193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7891ed69-db39-56d8-9b5d-8c5c52ec5455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388332} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd044fb-5944-5e08-96e0-0cdc5d5bbe18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9946a8e-68c1-5472-8dc1-edf6142ca046" :question/math-academy-id "q-135350" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101131 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100992 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e62b0e-adda-5d35-aeb9-961057dce8f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum or Difference of Three or More Matrices Using Distributivity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d0d5b8b-4428-5073-8c81-ebd4d03f5e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098122} {:answer/id #uuid "04d70404-4b26-53f0-9c5c-5e44fe5b9647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098123} {:answer/id #uuid "39e8426c-e203-5fdf-a93f-111238c8159f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098124} {:answer/id #uuid "71f20d62-7872-5e37-97e9-a23e08aef59f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098125} {:answer/id #uuid "75cc67b5-2545-59dc-9edf-f9e64c9bb09e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098126}] :answer-field/id #uuid "11b67b69-785c-5ae0-bd01-ea693dbbfc6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f88e9a5-8759-5e71-b262-00b079bef50f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388343} {:answer/id #uuid "f2609425-f61f-5689-a1b2-ad1766ba4f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388344} {:answer/id #uuid "065fbb44-49f9-5677-ae45-0db8eae4e9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388345} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7d6d9c-e6a7-5790-92dd-e8b2bca71761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388346} {:answer/id #uuid "b7fb0aa4-9a2d-5c94-a1be-3f68d1da0be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d7d6d9c-e6a7-5790-92dd-e8b2bca71761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388346} :answer-field/id #uuid "aefbe9b4-2591-5f99-bd99-dce5ef9f6719" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60ff0898-484c-5468-ab70-2a2b8951960b" :question/math-academy-id "q-13536" :question/problem "Find $(A+B)-C-(B-C)$, if\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)-C-(B-C) & =A+B-C-B+C \\\\  & =A+\\cancel{B}-\\cancel{C}-\\cancel{B}+\\cancel{C} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single matrix. So, the result is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6affd858-749d-5a94-854e-ddadd790ae45" :knowledge-point/title "Inverting a Permutation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b44952f5-62c3-54e0-971a-c074a603e5e4