:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b3e15ed-e7b6-5ea7-b9ed-17bf737d8274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266811} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a81cb7-756d-567d-b8be-538028bb5ed2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5606ff1-4177-5d4b-892b-30b0ba862cf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-136639" :question/problem "If $tan⁡a=\\frac{4}{5},$ then $tan⁡(-a)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-a) & =-tan⁡a \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184352 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114e3660-63d9-511d-b89c-e71081ffa1e5" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "037f04c8-ba6f-5b6c-8fa9-0c6883765bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266175} {:answer/id #uuid "4d76620b-4c1e-5237-a48c-f056d6dc9063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266833} {:answer/id #uuid "5079f712-46dd-55b7-8b26-77e72f0df867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266859} {:answer/id #uuid "50f90dfe-d802-574a-8ed8-759b5057b926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266869} {:answer/id #uuid "57c0df91-f04f-5221-8066-bed8410acb39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50f90dfe-d802-574a-8ed8-759b5057b926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266869} :answer-field/id #uuid "db7fea76-3c9e-5620-891f-f29f43564753" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b4cba33-ddfb-53fe-af87-4270187c1909" :question/math-academy-id "q-13751" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}}5x{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's introduce the new variable $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}}5x{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}}5{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}5{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(3-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(2) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a44b5058-f144-5b6a-b278-d37709c24ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116927} {:answer/id #uuid "a467653a-414d-5b69-930e-ddc2ab9ae250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116928} {:answer/id #uuid "e95757b7-75fc-5952-88e3-dc6d206d6640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116929} {:answer/id #uuid "2d709ef2-dee7-5bb2-a018-15cfe40e0232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116930} {:answer/id #uuid "663a032b-d529-58a1-a8d2-b550fb315588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116931}] :answer-field/id #uuid "514e70b3-6303-5301-bfda-6e0070e42283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76cc8a4b-832c-56c2-8cf5-70501cfbad40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396033} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6f508a-4794-5f61-a64e-b20147d225cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396034} {:answer/id #uuid "82b889e9-c745-5d62-97b1-40fc31c6e4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396035} {:answer/id #uuid "a128b52e-7259-5003-b476-9857977d9aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396036} {:answer/id #uuid "530ba56a-9b9f-5e98-981e-3ca0aa7acb9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82b889e9-c745-5d62-97b1-40fc31c6e4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396035} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc095a3a-82a7-5c30-b624-4fd7e0ceae34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6f9badf-44cd-56b4-946a-abae3220a5b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-13759" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${a}_{21}=3\\ne 0.$"}]}
